@startuml
title Replay map registration and log import

start
:Read cached replay-log response;
:Validate optional build IDs in map/game entries;
if (Valid map-state in response?) then (yes)
  :Compute canonical payload checksum\n(exclude top-level checksum field);
  if (Identical registered map?) then (yes)
    :Validate saved payload schema\nRequire embedded = registered = recalculated checksum;
  else (no)
    :Save map JSON with embedded checksum;
    :Validate saved payload schema\nRequire embedded = expected = recalculated checksum;
    :Register map ID and checksum;
  endif
  :Associate validated map with this replay as active;
endif
if (Active, validated map for this replay?) then (yes)
  :Reject a build ID conflicting with this replay;
  :Associate tagged build ID separately from map ID;
  if (Game-state entries?) then (yes)
    :Create JSONL with original lines;
    :Record map ID, checksum, file,\nresponse build ID and claim status;
  else (no)
    :Keep map registration and association only;
  endif
else (no)
  :Defer response without JSONL;
  :Retry after its replay map arrives;
endif
stop

@enduml
